uuid":"4c53c608-44da-4cdb-a3cc-a1d3d859d262","position":{"commit_sha":"52fdfe5d5ae6d5b26ea7d0b063eef743090b0ad2","position":"1794453887371565845-4c53c608-44da-4cdb-a3cc-a1d3d859d262"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Carry-over from the agentic engine arm (Gerrit 3354, nickel-ferric-llama, merged fdf0a94aba8): LLM-Review +1 with 7 ADVISORY findings, deliberately not re-pushed (a new patch set would reset both votes). They touch code this adapter replaces or extends:\n1. Stale comment in src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml above `engine_route` (~:58-62): it still says the route folds into ONE boolean and RAISES under agentic. The route now emits run_pipeline + run_agentic and never raises. Fix it when this story edits the agentic arm.\n2. The post-dispatch tail is now gated on engine == \"pipeline\" only, so under \"agentic\" a Layer-1 floor BLOCK with 2+ DET blockers skips fix-unit grouping. That only drops stamps; verdict and findings are identical. Decide whether floor verdicts should get the tail under both engines.\n3. A failed agent run degrades through `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (gate_dispatch.py ~:285), which records no `engine` and reports llm_ran False. The epic wants a non-clean agentic run to record `engine` and the failure class on coverage, so stamp coverage.engine=\"agentic\" on that path.\n4. No test pins that plan_review_agentic_verdict stamps the verdict `model` with the frontier class the agent ran on.\n5. test_prompt_is_packaged_and_free_of_bakeoff_placeholders asserts the prose \"dollar amounts\"; a wording check, not a contract.\n6. The prompt `plan-review-agentic` declares no `outputs:` front matter for `plan_review_agentic_findings`, unlike other structured plan-review-pass prompts. That affects prompt_override validation; add `outputs: plan_review_agentic_findings`.\n7. Same as 1, flagged as deletion impact.","timestamp":1794444373208188645},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 17:06 PST: OPEN, unsigned. Its prerequisite nickel-ferric-llama closed at 16:53 PST (merged fdf0a94aba8). First plan review (worktree CLI at fdf0a94aba8, Bedrock, 16:54-17:05 PST) returned BLOCK: 9 blocking and 20 advisory findings. They come down to 4 defects:\n(1) The plan says the adapted verdict flows through the \"unchanged post-dispatch path ... Pass-3 floors, advisory cap, sidecar emit and signing\". It doesn't: `_run_plan_review` runs `_apply_review_floors` only when engine == \"pipeline\", and the advisory cap lives in `orchestrator.partition_findings` (inside the pipeline's decide step), not after dispatch. State whether the adapter calls partition_findings/finalize_verdict with the cap, and whether the tail runs on agentic verdicts.\n(2) Tests outside Scope pin the interim behavior: tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py `_assert_agentic_indeterminate` and tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py assert INDETERMINATE plus `agentic-adapter-pending`. Add both to Scope. Also add src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py (`plan_review_agentic_verdict` is the op to replace) and the ADAPTER_PENDING_ID/coverage.agentic_findings references.\n(3) Failure handling: a failed agent step never reaches the adapter. It takes gate_dispatch's `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py), which records no `engine`. The epic wants engine plus failure class on coverage, so scope that path. There is no single \"resolution_class the pipeline uses\"; it is the closed failure-class enum from failure.outcome_of.\n(4) The \"unknown severity → advisory\" branch is unreachable, because the output contract already limits severity to the 4 values. Drop it or call it defensive. Cite partition_findings correctly (def ~:229) rather than finalize_verdict at :296-299.\nThe 7 carry-over advisories from change 3354 are in the previous comment. Next: revise the description (under 8,000 chars), then re-run review-plan. Not claimed.","timestamp":1794445589970162355}],"created_at":1794255883375978001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9a57c356-a20a-40fa-b981-81fa74203a4d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2473-79b7-1048-4a71"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBoth engines must produce one verdict contract, so the claim gate, `--status`, `sign-review` and MCP tools need no change. Today the agentic arm [rebar:nickel-ferric-llama] ends in `plan_review_agentic_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py`): an unsigned INDETERMINATE (`agentic-adapter-pending`). A failed agent step degrades with neither engine nor failure class: the interpreter keeps only the error string.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Adapter.** New `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py`, `adapt_findings(...)`, called by `plan_review_agentic_verdict` in place of the interim INDETERMINATE. It uses the pipeline's own two functions:\n- maps each agent finding: `finding` = `title` + `description`, `evidence` = `[evidence]`, `suggested_fix`, `criteria` filtered to ids in `registry.by_id()` (may be empty), `severity` kept, `tier: \"AGENTIC\"`, and `decision` from severity alone (ADR 0123; operator decision 2026-11-09): `blocker` → `\"block\"`, `major`/`minor`/`trivial` → `\"advisory\"`, and no `priority` (ADR 0123), so the stable advisory sort keeps the agent's order;\n- calls `orchestrator.partition_findings(det_blocking, det_advisory, mapped, advisory_cap=orchestrator.DEFAULT_ADVISORY_CAP)`, as `plan_review_decide` does (`decide_ops.py:266`), minting ids and narrowing duplicates;\n- calls `orchestrator.finalize_verdict` with `coaching=[]`, the agent's `provider_provenance`, coverage `{det, llm_ran: True, engine, hierarchy_incomplete(+_detail)}` and the frontier model. Zero blockers → PASS; any → BLOCK; `hierarchy_incomplete` → INDETERMINATE, as for the pipeline.\n\nThe verdict op gains inputs `provider_provenance` (from `steps.agentic_review.outputs`) and, from the precheck, `det_blocking`, `det_advisory`, `det_coverage`, `hierarchy_incomplete`, `hierarchy_incomplete_detail` (its input schema and the YAML step).\n\n**Post-dispatch path** in `_run_plan_review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`):\n1. It runs `_apply_review_floors` (Pass-3 floors, xcheck, fix-unit grouping) only under `engine == \"pipeline\"`. That stays: they judge Pass-2 fields the agent lacks and may make LLM sub-calls; the agentic engine is one call (ADR 0123). So an agentic floor BLOCK gets no fix-unit stamps (verdict unchanged).\n2. `_finalize_signature` signs a non-blocking PASS under either engine.\n3. `sidecar.emit` records it under both; sidecar readers (prior concerns, novelty, status) see agentic findings too, as intended.\n\n**Reuse shortcuts** (`reuse.py`; `drift_refresh` is in `orchestrator.py`) still run only under `engine == \"pipeline\"`:\n- `verdict_reuse` replays a stored BLOCK sidecar's findings as the review's result. It returns None when that same sidecar's `coverage.engine` is non-pipeline (absent = pipeline). A pipeline run thus never presents agentic blockers as its own.\n- `idempotent_reuse` and `drift_refresh` are gated by the current attestation and stay engine-agnostic: a PASS attestation is the same certification under either engine (ADR 0123), and `idempotent_reuse` fires exactly when a claim would pass, so a pipeline run on an agentic-certified ticket reports `idempotent_skip`. [rebar:foliated-oceangoing-parrot] records the signer on the attestation; inferring it from unbound sidecars is rejected.\n\n**Failed runs** fail the `agentic_review` step and never reach the adapter.\n- `RunnerAgentStep` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py`) keeps the last exception its runner raised (`last_error`). Under `engine == \"agentic\"`, `produce_plan_review_verdict` (`gate_dispatch.py`, 2 lines) passes `plan_review_recovery.agentic_failure_error(last_error, res.error)` to `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` instead of the string. The new helper (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`) keeps an existing `outcome`, else attaches one: an `UnretryableOutputError` whose new `stop_reason` attribute (set where `structured.check_stop_reason`/`check_response` raise it, `src/rebar/llm/structured.py`) is `refusal`/`content_filter` → rewrapped as `LLMInputRejectedError` with CHANGE_INPUT (so `input_rejected`), `max_tokens`/`length` → CHANGE_SETTINGS. A prompted-path truncation is retried in-run (`pai_retry.concision_guard`); exhausted retries raise a reason-less `UnretryableOutputError` (`structured_run._exhausted_output_retries`) → NEEDS_INVESTIGATION; `LLMBudgetExhaustedError`/`RunawayToolLoopError` → FIX_AGENT_DESIGN; otherwise `failure.classify_llm_failure` on its `__cause__` or itself (unmatched → NEEDS_INVESTIGATION). With no `last_error` (a scripted agentic step failed), an `LLMUnavailableError` of the step error with NEEDS_INVESTIGATION. So every failed agentic run records a class.\n- `_run_plan_review` stamps `coverage.engine = engine` on every non-pipeline verdict (floor, adapted, degraded); pipeline coverage is unchanged.\n\n**Change-3354 advisories:** fix the stale `engine_route` YAML comment; add `outputs: plan_review_agentic_findings` to the prompt; test the verdict `model` (frontier); drop the \"dollar amounts\" assertion. Severity is limited to four values, so no unknown-severity branch.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py (new)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py, runs.py, plan_review_recovery.py; src/rebar/llm/structured.py\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_agentic_verdict_input.schema.json\n- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md\n- docs/config.md (agentic verdicts now PASS/BLOCK)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py (new), tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py (new)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py, tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py (replace the interim INDETERMINATE/`agentic-adapter-pending` assertions)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Worked examples via `review_plan(engine=\"agentic\")` with a FakeRunner: `[blocker, major]` → BLOCK with 1 blocking and 1 advisory, unsigned; `[major, trivial]` → PASS with 2 advisories in that order, signed, and `review-plan --status` reports `certified`; `[]` → PASS. Criteria outside the registry are dropped from a finding.\n- Failure (each INDETERMINATE, `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`, zero attestations): outcome-carrying `LLMUnavailableError` → its class; refusal and content-filter turns → CHANGE_INPUT + `input_rejected`; a stop-reason truncation → CHANGE_SETTINGS, an exhausted-retry one → NEEDS_INVESTIGATION; budget and tool-loop → FIX_AGENT_DESIGN; plain `RuntimeError`, `FindingsError` and a failing inputs op → NEEDS_INVESTIGATION.\n- Floor verdicts carry `coverage.engine` under agentic; `hierarchy_incomplete` → INDETERMINATE.\n- Reuse: after an agentic BLOCK, a pipeline review runs the pipeline (no `verdict_reuse`); a pipeline BLOCK is still reused; after an agentic PASS, a pipeline review reports `idempotent_skip` with the attestation unchanged.\n- Pipeline coverage: no `engine` key.\n- Schema parity: pipeline and agentic FakeRunner verdicts both validate against `plan_review_verdict.schema.json`. Both sidecar payloads have schema `plan_review_result_v2`, the same top-level keys, and read back via `sidecar.latest_review_result`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The severity mapping, field mapping, PASS signing, failure class, engine stamp and BLOCK-reuse engine match are pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`.\n- [ ] Both engines' verdicts and sidecars satisfy the same contracts, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` describes agentic PASS/BLOCK; `grep -c \"outputs: plan_review_agentic_findings\" src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md` prints 1.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`, and no `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py","reason":"new adapter"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py","reason":"verdict op calls adapter"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"engine stamp"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py","reason":"verdict_reuse engine match"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"agentic degrade error"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py","reason":"RunnerAgentStep.last_error"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py","reason":"agentic_failure_error helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured.py","reason":"UnretryableOutputError.stop_reason"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml","reason":"verdict inputs, comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_agentic_verdict_input.schema.json","reason":"new inputs"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md","reason":"outputs front matter"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"engine doc"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py","reason":"interim assertions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py","reason":"interim assertions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2473-79b7-1048-4a71"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"2c23a520-6486-4796-84b6-e82ef460a9a9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f","ticket_type":"story","title":"Agentic verdict adapter: map agent findings onto the plan_review_verdict and REVIEW_RESULT schemas","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["72206832-a89d-40bb-9b0a-a1ff29cbd007","8651e518-d5bb-41a2-869e-8e586fab670a","bb2321b3-c2d5-49d3-8c6d-811d89f1da69","c1712578-5a7f-4f42-8d78-21e92a39c3b2","80fcd72e-501f-43e2-b2f0-c40c7caad8b9","12a990eb-fcb7-4470-8bc8-3a511dc87a8d","1e3e4c2f-9038-4bf1-9180-431333bedea4","cf3e21be-46ee-49c4-9e73-5988750c01bc","a2862e85-a3e4-4062-8403-8858f15388da","7131e9de-dbd1-4497-ac98-8f5ad33f582d","24f90fc4-7162-4c1c-a7ac-f4556dc91fca","034e6ef6-3d42-45d5-9a7d-24b5db557a7d","f58b2d2d-14b3-483d-b3cd-b9dde01d5f32","d23eb9b5-83f9-43fe-bc23-390bd3418ff6","aefa2874-6026-4a1e-9a6b-3e29d394bece","2c23a520-6486-4796-84b6-e82ef460a9a9","4c53c608-44da-4cdb-a3cc-a1d3d859d262"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794453887371565846,"uuid":"669e4b5d-8792-46e5-857f-acdfdf358417"}